From b247df58ecc6ff19d940ce7d380d8587b48b482f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:36:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/20] feat(deployment): let a fake instance exit on request

The controller now finds instances that stopped running and redeploys
their services, but a fake instance only ends with the control plane
process, so nothing outside the unit tests can make one disappear
while the control plane keeps running. The compose smoke needs that to
check the lost-instance path end to end.

POST /fake/exit on a fake instance makes it end like an exited
process: the launcher forgets it before answering 202, so is_running
is false from then on, and it then stops listening and interrupts its
other requests. The request itself is left out of the interruption so
the caller gets its answer. aclose waits for instances that are still
exiting, so closing the launcher leaves no task behind.

Only fake instances have the route, and the gateway forwards to the
fixed path of an endpoint's protocol, so it cannot be reached through
the gateway.
